   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Image\n",
    "from src.clean import load_crashes, parse_hhmm, tableau_export\n",
    "from src.eda import create_eda\n",
    "from src.model import train_and_evaluate\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "OUTPUT = ROOT / 'outputs'\n",
    "OUTPUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a6f904f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Clean and manage the data\n",
    "\n",
    "Use the single 2024\u20132025 snapshot. Retain **24 relevant source fields** and validate that **CASE_ID identifies one crash**. Trim whitespace, standardize blanks, and validate dates, county, and severity. These steps are implemented in [src/clean.py](src/clean.py); the [cleaning decisions](data/README.md) explain why each is necessary.\n",
    "\n",
    "Define severe/fatal as severity codes **1 or 2**. Keep the recorded-crash denominator beside each proportion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "862b7ed1",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T04:58:55.253023Z",
