  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b78cda2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Why keep CASE_ID?** Two distinct crashes can have identical selected attributes. Dropping duplicates after removing the ID could erase real events. We preserve identity throughout preparation, then select the dashboard fields at export. Coordinate and time exclusions overlap, so they cannot simply be added."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "510ff519",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Explore counts and severity shares\n",
    "\n",
    "**Count** shows observed volume. **Severity share** shows the proportion of recorded injury crashes that were severe/fatal. The dataset has no traffic-exposure denominator, so neither is a per-journey crash risk.\n",
    "\n",
    "The five time blocks reproduce the Tableau categories. Their durations differ; block counts are not hourly rates."
   ]
  },
