   "source": [
    "## 3. Evaluate one random forest\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question:** How well can the existing model distinguish severe/fatal from other injury crashes?\n",
    "\n",
    "| Decision | Implementation |\n",
    "| --- | --- |\n",
    "| Target | Severe/fatal = 1; other injury = 0 |\n",
    "| Features | Calendar variables, cyclical time encodings, and intersection/highway/control-device/hit-and-run flags |\n",
    "| Split | Sort by crash datetime; earliest 80% for training, latest 20% for testing |\n",
    "| Imbalance | Balanced class weights; about 11% of crashes are severe |\n",
    "| Model | Original random forest: 300 trees, max depth 12, minimum split 10, minimum leaf 5, seed 42 |\n",
    "| Evaluation | Fixed 0.50 threshold; ROC AUC, trapezoidal PR AUC, severe precision/recall, confusion matrix |\n",
    "\n",
    "The original settings are retained; no new tuning is performed. [src/model.py](src/model.py) contains the complete process. Eligibility additionally requires the original modeling fields to be present. Some inputs, especially hit-and-run status, are recorded after a crash; this is a retrospective severity classifier."
   ]
  },
